  "plain": "The CIA, America's main foreign spy agency, was formed in the 1940s at the urging of Brown Brothers Harriman, a private investment firm. Michels says this is the core of a history of American intelligence by a man named Dan Sheehan, covering the years after the OSS, the US spy service of the Second World War. Michels raises it in a talk with the analyst Matthew Pines to suggest that private money helped shape the secret side of government from the start."
